.TH "CONDINAPT\-MINIOS" "7" "September 2026" "MiniOS CondinAPT Integration" ""
.SH NAME
condinapt\-minios \- use CondinAPT in MiniOS build modules
.SH DESCRIPTION
MiniOS modules use \f[B]condinapt\f[R](1) to select and install APT
packages from the active build configuration.
This page documents the MiniOS staging paths, module layout, and
standard filter map.
.SH MODULE INTEGRATION
The builder discovers modules through the selected environment
directory:
.IP
.EX
linux\-live/environments/<desktop>/
.EE
.PP
Entries there are normally links to reusable module sources under:
.IP
.EX
linux\-live/scripts/<NN\-module\-name>/
.EE
.PP
During the install stage, the builder copies the module\[cq]s
\f[B]install\f[R] script to \f[B]/install\f[R] in the chroot.
It also stages \f[B]condinapt\f[R], \f[B]condinapt.map\f[R],
\f[B]packages.list\f[R], and the generated build configuration at the
chroot root.
Do not rely on \f[B]$CWD\f[R] or an installed
\f[B]/usr/share/minios\-live\f[R] path from inside a module script.
.PP
A minimal \f[B]install\f[R] script is:
.IP
.EX
#!/bin/bash
set \-e
set \-o pipefail
set \-u

\&. /minioslib || exit 1
\&. /minios_build.conf || exit 1

SCRIPT_DIR=\[dq]$(dirname \[dq]$(readlink \-f \[dq]$0\[dq])\[dq])\[dq]
/condinapt \[rs]
    \-l \[dq]${SCRIPT_DIR}/packages.list\[dq] \[rs]
    \-c \[dq]${SCRIPT_DIR}/minios_build.conf\[dq] \[rs]
    \-m \[dq]${SCRIPT_DIR}/condinapt.map\[dq]
.EE
.PP
The standard module may contain:
.IP
.EX
NN\-module\-name/
|\-\- packages.list
|\-\- install
|\-\- skip_conditions.conf       # optional
|\-\- rootcopy\-install/          # optional
|\-\- build                      # optional
|\-\- patches/                   # optional, used by build
|\-\- is_dkms_build              # optional DKMS marker
|\-\- rootcopy\-postinstall/      # optional
\[ga]\-\- postinstall                # optional
.EE
.PP
See \f[B]linux\-live/scripts/10\-example/README.md\f[R] for the complete
module lifecycle, ownership manifests, naming, and environment\-link
instructions.
.SH MINIOS FILTER MAP
The current \f[B]linux\-live/condinapt.map\f[R] contains:
.IP
.EX
d=DISTRIBUTION
da=DISTRIBUTION_ARCH
dp=DISTRIBUTION_PROFILE
is=INIT_SYSTEM
de=DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENT
pv=PACKAGE_VARIANT
ik=INSTALL_KERNEL
kf=KERNEL_FLAVOUR
kp=KERNEL_PROVIDER
ks=KERNEL_SERIES
kc=KERNEL_CAPABILITIES
kbd=KERNEL_BUILD_DKMS
ib=INITRAMFS_BUILDER
lo=LOCALE
ml=MULTILINGUAL
kl=KEEP_LOCALES
.EE
.PP
Scalar filters use exact string equality.
Inside the \f[B]01\-kernel\f[R] build flow,
\f[B]KERNEL_CAPABILITIES\f[R] is an indexed Bash array, so \f[B]kc\f[R]
matches any detected capability.
The \f[B]ks\f[R] and \f[B]kc\f[R] values are not available to ordinary
later modules.
.SH CONFIGURATION VALUES
The default \f[B]build.conf\f[R] currently lists:
.TP
\f[B]DISTRIBUTION\f[R]
Debian \f[B]buster\f[R], \f[B]bullseye\f[R], \f[B]bookworm\f[R],
\f[B]trixie\f[R]; Ubuntu \f[B]bionic\f[R], \f[B]focal\f[R],
\f[B]jammy\f[R], \f[B]noble\f[R], \f[B]resolute\f[R]; or Devuan
\f[B]beowulf\f[R], \f[B]chimaera\f[R], \f[B]daedalus\f[R],
\f[B]excalibur\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]DISTRIBUTION_ARCH\f[R]
\f[B]amd64\f[R], \f[B]i386\f[R], or \f[B]i386\-pae\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENT\f[R]
\f[B]core\f[R], \f[B]flux\f[R], \f[B]xfce\f[R], or \f[B]lxqt\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]PACKAGE_VARIANT\f[R]
\f[B]minimum\f[R], \f[B]standard\f[R], \f[B]toolbox\f[R], or
\f[B]ultra\f[R].
The builder normalizes Flux to \f[B]minimum\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]INSTALL_KERNEL\f[R]
Whether to install a kernel.
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_PROVIDER\f[R]
\f[B]distribution\f[R] or \f[B]minios\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]MINIOS_KERNEL_SERIES\f[R]
User selection for the MiniOS provider: \f[B]auto\f[R], \f[B]6.1\f[R],
or \f[B]6.12\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_FLAVOUR\f[R]
\f[B]none\f[R], \f[B]rt\f[R], or \f[B]cloud\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_BUILD_DKMS\f[R]
Whether to build additional DKMS drivers.
.TP
\f[B]INITRAMFS_BUILDER\f[R]
\f[B]livekit\f[R] or \f[B]dracut\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]LOCALE\f[R], \f[B]MULTILINGUAL\f[R], \f[B]KEEP_LOCALES\f[R]
Locale selection and locale\-retention settings.
.PP
CondinAPT can use an unmapped full variable name only when that variable
is present in the configuration supplied with \f[B]\-c\f[R].
The generated module configuration includes selected distribution,
compression, kernel, locale, timezone, user, and builder values.
It does not include every \f[B]build.conf\f[R] value; boot\-loader,
menu, persistence, snapshot, and most cache or debugging settings are
unavailable to ordinary module calls unless a module supplies them
explicitly.
.SH DERIVED VALUES
.TP
\f[B]DISTRIBUTION_PROFILE\f[R]
Behavior profile derived from the selected suite, normally
\f[B]debian\f[R] or \f[B]ubuntu\f[R].
Devuan suites use the Debian profile.
.TP
\f[B]INIT_SYSTEM\f[R]
Derived init\-system profile, normally \f[B]systemd\f[R] or
\f[B]sysvinit\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_SERIES\f[R] and \f[B]KERNEL_CAPABILITIES\f[R]
Resolved kernel values appended to a temporary configuration used only
by CondinAPT calls inside the \f[B]01\-kernel\f[R] build flow.
\f[B]MINIOS_KERNEL_SERIES\f[R] is the user setting;
\f[B]KERNEL_SERIES\f[R] is the detected series used by \f[B]ks\f[R].
Neither \f[B]ks\f[R] nor \f[B]kc\f[R] is propagated to ordinary later
modules.
.SH PACKAGE LIST EXAMPLES
Install additional codecs except in the minimum variant:
.IP
.EX
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-base
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-good
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-bad \-pv=minimum
gstreamer1.0\-libav \-pv=minimum
.EE
.PP
Select applications by variant and desktop:
.IP
.EX
audacity +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra}
kdenlive +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra} +{de=xfce|de=lxqt}
.EE
.PP
Select a target release:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg \[at]bookworm\-backports +d=bookworm
.EE
.PP
Inside \f[B]linux\-live/scripts/01\-kernel/packages.list\f[R], exclude
DKMS packages when the selected kernel already has the capability:
.IP
.EX
ntfs3\-dkms \-kc=ntfs3
aufs\-dkms \-kc=aufs +kbd=true
.EE
.PP
Choose a package during planning, not after an APT transaction failure:
.IP
.EX
exfatprogs || exfat\-utils && exfat\-fuse
.EE
.SH REBUILDING MODULES
\f[B]build\-modules\f[R] skips a module whose SquashFS artifact is
already present.
After changing a module, remove its existing artifact from the selected
work directory\[cq]s \f[B]image/\f[R] tree and rerun \f[B]minios\-live
build\-modules\f[R].
The builder invalidates the following non\-kernel module chain once an
artifact is missing.
Kernel module rebuilding follows separate handling in the builder.
